    goal: 'Build a real lighthouse with its keeper cottage on the north-east headland. The tower is climbed by four straight flights through the three floors below the top to the lantern room, then up to a walkable gallery deck around a cone cap. The contact board in the lantern room opens the contact dialogue (LinkedIn, GitHub, email click-to-reveal; no phone number). The keeper cottage at the foot of the tower has a living-kitchen room and a bedroom. The tower looks round from outside: a cylinder skin over a square structural shell. Also prove journey 4 (walk the road from the harbour, climb, read the board).',
